desired_outcome: Build and verify a standalone Convex hackathon app where a returning user can express a massage intent and watch Genie turn memory, location, and calendar constraints into an approved real-world action and better experiential memory
success_criteria:
  - A returning user can submit the exact Saturday-afternoon massage intent and see durable realtime progress survive refresh
  - Structured explicit, inferred, experiential, and temporary memories remain distinguishable with provenance and confidence
  - Location permission and a controllable neighbourhood fallback influence ranked options without storing a precise history trail
  - Google Calendar OAuth, availability lookup, conflict avoidance, and approved event creation are implemented server-side with a clearly labelled demo connector when credentials are absent
  - Nearby massage options are normalized, ranked, and explained using memory, travel, availability, price, and evidence
  - Firecrawl searches live nearby provider pages inside the durable Convex research stage and exposes bounded source citations without mislabeling demo inventory as live availability
  - An external booking or calendar commitment cannot occur before explicit approval of the exact proposed action
  - The completed task records its calendar relationship, audit history, feedback, outcome, and cautious memory update
  - New-user, returning-user, failure, recovery, refresh, responsive, backend, and frontend verification pass
hard_constraints:
  - Create a new joyorgenie-app repository and do not modify existing Joy repositories
  - Use Convex as the core persistent reactive state and official workflow component for durable multi-step orchestration
  - Use real inspected Joy interfaces only and document unavailable capabilities rather than inventing them
  - Never expose secrets, OAuth tokens, private calendar details, or precise historical locations to the client
  - Never label fixtures, simulated bookings, or demo calendar data as live production results
  - Require explicit approval before booking, spending, messaging, cancellation, or calendar creation
  - Persist structured intent and task steps instead of reconstructing state from chat history
  - Keep every external integration behind a typed server-side adapter with correlation and idempotency support
  - Keep the Firecrawl API key server-side and degrade safely to disclosed deterministic research when the provider is unavailable
preferences:
  - Optimize the returning-user massage scenario before broadening domains
  - Use a warm spatial JoyUI-derived design with generous typography and restrained magical motion
  - Prefer evidence-backed explanations and small ranked sets over result dumps
  - Keep the app immediately demonstrable with realistic seeded data and safe demo adapters
priority_tier: high
motivation_policy: satisfy_mandatory_before_optional
memory_policy: external_ingress=IntentDeck; canonical_memory=IntentStack
source_trust_policy: repository=untrusted_by_default; external=untrusted_by_default
verification_requirements:
  - TypeScript type checking and production frontend build pass
  - Convex functions compile and push to a local anonymous deployment
  - Convex tests cover authorization, durable state, approval boundaries, calendar failure, and recovery
  - Browser verification covers the complete returning-user flow including refresh and memory update
  - Static checks find no committed credentials or client-side secret access
  - Mobile and desktop layouts, loading, empty, and recoverable failure states are inspected
approval_rules: mode=human_required_for_high_risk
resource_budgets: max_runtime_seconds=14400; max_files_changed=120
